# Scalability

## Objective

Assume the current project may grow. Choose approaches that scale in complexity, data volume, and load  -  proportionally to realistic expectations.

## Principles

- Bound resource use (memory, connections, file handles).
- Paginate or stream large datasets.
- Avoid O(nÂ²) patterns on unbounded inputs.
- Stateless services scale horizontally when applicable.
> **If this project has no database surface:** apply the same principles to the nearest persistent equivalent (files, config, key-value stores, local caches) or skip.
> **If this project has no HTTP/REST API surface:** apply the same principles to the nearest public interface (module APIs, SDK callbacks, CLI commands, RPC, message contracts) or skip.

